-- ============================================================================
-- 30 - The seven languages
-- ============================================================================
-- Enabling a language is what makes a build emit anything for it. A translation
-- written against a language that is not in this list is stored, passes
-- `mx check`, and is silently discarded at build time — no
-- translations_<code>.properties is produced at all. So this file has to run
-- before 31-translations-*.mdl, and the numbering says so.
--
-- CheckCompleteness is deliberately left at its default (false) on every
-- language added here. Turning it on reports an error for every string with no
-- translation in that language, and this app has roughly 400 of them across
-- seven languages — the pane would be unreadable and `mx check` would fail on
-- work that is deliberately partial (see 31-translations-*.mdl on what is
-- translated and what is not). It is the right setting for an app that intends
-- to ship every language complete; it is the wrong setting for a demonstration.
--
-- en_US stays the default. Mendix always checks the default language for
-- completeness regardless of this flag, which is another reason to leave the
-- rest off: the language whose strings are actually all present is the one
-- being checked.
-- ============================================================================

alter settings LANGUAGE add or modify 'nl_NL';
/
alter settings LANGUAGE add or modify 'de_DE';
/
alter settings LANGUAGE add or modify 'fr_FR';
/
alter settings LANGUAGE add or modify 'cs_CZ';
/
alter settings LANGUAGE add or modify 'es_ES';
/
alter settings LANGUAGE add or modify 'it_IT';
/

-- Re-stated rather than assumed: `add or modify` on a language that is already
-- present leaves the default alone, but the default is what every untranslated
-- string falls back to, so it is worth being explicit about which one it is.
alter settings LANGUAGE
  DefaultLanguageCode = 'en_US';
/
